WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:08.610
There is a battle for control in Iran
between far-right hardliners and

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.690
relative moderates. Hardliners generally
support aggressive foreign policy and

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.139
reject even limited political and
economic freedoms. Moderates

00:00:16.139 --> 00:00:19.859
contrastingly support the Iran nuclear
deal and some economic reform, like more

00:00:19.859 --> 00:00:23.789
trade with Europe. But in Iran's 2020
parliamentary elections the regime

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:28.439
disqualified most moderate candidates
and hardliners won. Turnout hit historic

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:33.480
lows. Iranians are angry with the unfair
elections. In 2019, moderates headed

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.059
Iran's three government branches.
Hardliners will control two in 2020. If a

00:00:39.059 --> 00:00:43.530
far-right candidate becomes president in
2021 — which is likely — they will head all

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:48.210
three branches. Growing hardliner control
will facilitate more aggressive and

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.719
authoritarian behavior. The Islamic
Revolutionary Guards Corps would further

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:56.160
destabilize the region and oppress Iran's
populace, likely exacerbating domestic

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.000
anger with the regime. Iran's political
landscape is changing profoundly and

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.199
there's trouble ahead for Iran's people,
the Middle East, and yes, most probably

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:06.540
the United States.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.950
Do you think a hardliner will win Iran's

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.120
presidential election in 2021? Let us
know in our poll. Also, let us know what

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.420
other topics you'd like our scholars to
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.940
and subscribe for more research and
videos from AEI.

